<BaseLayout title="About | Megan Lange">
  <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>

  <p class="intro">
    Product manager known for turning ambiguous, cross-organizational problems into clear
    product strategy, aligned technical designs, and measurable customer and business outcomes.
    I&rsquo;ve spent most of my career deep in commerce platforms, and I&rsquo;m most useful
    where the problem is tangled and the path isn&rsquo;t obvious yet. After being impacted by
    <a href="https://news.xbox.com/en-us/2026/07/06/resetting-xbox/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
      >Microsoft&rsquo;s July 2026 layoff</a>, I&rsquo;m looking for new product areas to bring
    that to.
  </p>

  <h2>Bio</h2>
  <p>
    Senior product leader with 12+ years building commerce platform capabilities and experiences
    across Xbox, Microsoft 365, and Windows devices &mdash; the systems that handle everything
    from how something is priced to how a customer pays, when a subscription renews, and how
    regulatory compliance shapes what markets a business can operate in. My scope has spanned
    core purchase, checkout, subscriptions, partner channels, and regulated payments.
  </p>
  <p>
    Before Microsoft, I was Program Manager (later Senior Program Manager) at DatStat, Inc., a
    Seattle-based health-tech startup I joined as an intern in 2014 while finishing my B.S. in
    Informatics at the University of Washington. I was the engineering team&rsquo;s first PM,
    established their agile practices, and built DatStat Connect &mdash; a clinical-research and
    care-plan platform &mdash; from concept through launch. It went on to run studies for the
    COPD Foundation, Group Health Cooperative, Seattle Children&rsquo;s Hospital, and the Ontario
    HIV Treatment Network. When DatStat was acquired in April 2018, I decided it was time for
    something new.
  </p>
  <p>
    I joined Microsoft in August 2018 as a Program Manager in commercial commerce, where I owned
    modernizing the transactional email and notification system: I built a new service and drove
    the migration off Salesforce onto internal infrastructure, cutting the maintenance surface by
    72%. That work also turned self-serve cancellation into a retention channel and lifted signup
    conversion on Teams. The systems built there are still leveraged across both the consumer and
    commercial platforms today.
  </p>
  <p>
    In March 2021 I moved to the Consumer Commerce Platform team, and over the following five
    years grew from single-capability ownership to cross-cutting programs spanning multiple
    engineering pillars and business areas &mdash; eventually serving as purchase team lead
    across purchase, order management, payments, catalog, and the OEM device channel. Along the
    way I took a device-bundling program its biggest OEMs had written off and grew it into a $98M
    business, delivered the platform side of Rockstar&rsquo;s GTA VI pre-order launch in 20+
    countries, and redesigned how money moves through the consumer platform end to end in support
    of changing payment service regulations.
  </p>
  <p>
    My strengths lie in driving clarity through complexity: designing the forums that get the
    right people talking, facilitating alignment across cross-functional stakeholders, and
    translating ambiguous regulatory or business requirements into concrete engineering work.
    I&rsquo;m also an AI-native PM in practice &mdash; I build the tooling my teammates adopt
    into daily use, and I mentor teams and leadership on AI adoption.
  </p>

  <h2>How I Work</h2>
  <p class="section-note">
    Recurring themes across 54 peer perspectives &mdash; engineers, PMs, marketers, finance,
    support, and partner leads &mdash; from Microsoft&rsquo;s Connect review process, FY25&ndash;FY26.
  </p>
  <ul class="traits">
    {howIWork.map((t) => (
      <li>
        <strong>{t.theme}</strong>
        <span class="quote">&ldquo;{t.quote}&rdquo;</span>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <h2>Timeline</h2>
